{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Of David. To You, O YHWH, I lift my soul.</b> Rabbi Moses said: the sense of 'my soul I lift' is like the wave-offering, as: 'and he shall lift [ונשא] heave-offerings' [Leviticus 7:14]. But what is correct in my eyes: it is like 'and to Him one lifts his soul' [cf. Psalm 25:1], and not to another."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:28.972963256Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}